1
00:00:02,586 --> 00:00:04,254
( BIRDS SQUAWKING )

2
00:00:13,472 --> 00:00:14,723
( CAWING )

3
00:00:17,768 --> 00:00:19,436
( WINGS FLUTTERING )

4
00:00:31,949 --> 00:00:33,283
( CHIRPING )

5
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:35,869
( TWITTERING )

6
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:35,095
( SQUAWKING INTENSIFIES )

7
00:01:46,982 --> 00:01:48,942
( CABLE CAR BELL DINGING )

8
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,744
( SQUAWKING CONTINUES )

9
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:09,087
( BOY WOLF WHISTLES )

10
00:02:11,214 --> 00:02:12,883
( BIRDS SQUAWKING )

11
00:02:23,185 --> 00:02:24,770
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

12
00:02:30,817 --> 00:02:32,027
Hello , Mrs. MacGruder .

13
00:02:32,069 --> 00:02:33,195
Oh , hello , Miss Daniels .

14
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:36,365
Have you ever seen so many gulls ? What do you suppose it is ?

15
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:40,452
There must be a storm at sea . That can drive them inland , you know .

16
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:44,081
I was hoping you 'd be a little late . You see , he hasn 't arrived yet .

17
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:46,083
- Oh , but you said 3 : 00 . - Oh , I know .

18
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:48,960
I know . I 've been calling all morning .

19
00:02:49,044 --> 00:02:51,296
Oh , Miss Daniels , you have no idea .

20
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:54,132
They are so difficult to get . Really , they are .

21
00:02:54,216 --> 00:02:55,425
We have to get them from India ,

22
00:02:55,509 --> 00:02:57,052
when they 're just baby chicks , and then ...

23
00:02:57,094 --> 00:02:59,054
This one won 't be a chick , will he ?

24
00:02:59,221 --> 00:03:01,598
Certainly not . Oh , no , certainly not .

25
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,475
This will be a full-grown mynah bird . Full-grown .

26
00:03:04,101 --> 00:03:05,185
And he 'll talk ?

27
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:07,437
Well , yes , of course he 'll ...

28
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:10,899
Well , no , you 'll have to teach him to talk .

29
00:03:10,982 --> 00:03:15,112
I guess maybe I 'd better phone . They said 3 : 00 .

30
00:03:15,153 --> 00:03:17,948
Maybe it 's the traffic . I 'll call .

31
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:19,282
Would you mind waiting ?

32
00:03:19,366 --> 00:03:21,493
Well , maybe you 'd better deliver him .

33
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:23,578
Let me give you my address .

34
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,164
Oh , well , all right ,

35
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:28,959
but I 'm sure they 're on the way .

36
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,670
Would you mind if I called ?

37
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:33,672
No . All right .

38
00:03:51,148 --> 00:03:52,816
MITCH : I wonder if you could help me .

39
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:53,942
What ?

40
00:03:55,277 --> 00:03:56,570
I said , I wonder if you could help me .

41
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,492
Yes . What is it you 're looking for , sir ?

42
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:04,578
Lovebirds .

43
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:06,163
Lovebirds , sir ?

44
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,206
Yes . I understand there are different varieties .

45
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:09,332
Is that true ?

46
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,625
Well , yes , there are .

47
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:13,545
Well , these are for my sister for her birthday , you see ,

48
00:04:13,628 --> 00:04:15,505
and as she 's only gonna be 11 ,

49
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:16,798
I wouldn 't want a pair of birds

50
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:19,509
that were too demonstrative .

51
00:04:19,551 --> 00:04:20,844
I understand completely .

52
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:23,680
At the same time , I wouldn 't want them to be too aloof , either .

53
00:04:23,764 --> 00:04:25,432
No , of course not .

54
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:28,685
Do you happen to have a pair of birds that are just friendly ?

55
00:04:28,769 --> 00:04:33,565
Oh , I think so . Now , then , let me see .

56
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:39,988
Aren 't those lovebirds ?

57
00:04:40,864 --> 00:04:43,742
No . Those are red birds .

58
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:46,244
I thought they were strawberry finches .

59
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:48,872
Yes . We call them that , too .

60
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:52,959
Here we are . Lovebirds .

61
00:04:54,586 --> 00:04:56,546
Those are canaries .

62
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:59,007
Doesn 't this make you feel awful ?

63
00:04:59,049 --> 00:05:00,509
Doesn 't what make me feel ...

64
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:03,762
Having all these poor , little innocent creatures caged up like this ?

65
00:05:03,845 --> 00:05:06,640
Well , we can 't just let them fly around the shop , you know .

66
00:05:06,723 --> 00:05:07,849
( CHUCKLING ) No , I suppose not .

67
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:09,976
Is there an ornithological reason

68
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:12,187
for keeping them in separate cages ?

69
00:05:12,229 --> 00:05:14,523
Well , certainly . It 's to protect the species .

70
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:17,192
Yes , that 's important , especially during the molting season .

71
00:05:17,234 --> 00:05:19,903
That 's a particularly dangerous time .

72
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,905
Are they molting now ?

73
00:05:21,947 --> 00:05:23,406
Oh , some of them are .

74
00:05:23,907 --> 00:05:24,991
How can you tell ?

75
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:30,664
Well , they get a sort of hangdog expression .

76
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:36,336
Yes , I see . Well , what about the lovebirds ?

77
00:05:36,419 --> 00:05:38,672
Are you sure you wouldn 't like to see a canary instead ?

78
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:41,174
We have some very nice canaries this week .

79
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:42,759
All right .

80
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:45,929
All right . May I see it , please ?

81
00:06:00,610 --> 00:06:01,820
Oh ! Oh !

82
00:06:03,113 --> 00:06:05,240
Oh , what is it ? Oh !

83
00:06:19,588 --> 00:06:21,506
MITCH : There we are .

84
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:23,466
- Oh , there . - Wonderful .

85
00:06:26,636 --> 00:06:29,139
Back in your gilded cage , Melanie Daniels .

86
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:31,975
What did you say ?

87
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:35,312
I was merely drawing a parallel , Miss Daniels .

88
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:36,980
How did you know my name ?

89
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:39,065
A little birdie told me .

90
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:41,568
Good day , Miss Daniels . Madam .

91
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,361
Hey , wait a minute .

92
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:45,780
I don 't know you .

93
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:47,282
Ah , but I know you .

94
00:06:47,324 --> 00:06:48,491
How ?

95
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:49,576
We met in court .

96
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:52,287
We never met in court or anyplace else .

97
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:54,164
That 's true . I 'll rephrase it . I saw you in court .

98
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,373
When ?

99
00:06:55,457 --> 00:06:57,667
Don 't you remember one of your practical jokes

100
00:06:57,751 --> 00:06:59,628
that resulted in the smashing of a plate-glass window ?

101
00:06:59,669 --> 00:07:01,588
I didn 't break that window .

102
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:03,214
Yes , but your little prank did .

103
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:05,091
The judge should 've put you behind bars .

104
00:07:05,175 --> 00:07:07,844
What are you , a policeman ?

105
00:07:07,928 --> 00:07:09,679
I merely believe in the law , Miss Daniels .

106
00:07:09,721 --> 00:07:11,806
And I 'm not too keen on practical jokers .

107
00:07:11,848 --> 00:07:13,183
What do you call your lovebird story if not ...

108
00:07:13,767 --> 00:07:15,518
Oh , I really wanted the lovebirds .

109
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,355
Well , you knew I didn 't work here . You deliberately ...

110
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:20,482
Right . I recognized you when I came in .

111
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:22,192
I just thought you might like to know

112
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:23,902
what it 's like to be on the other end of a gag .

113
00:07:23,985 --> 00:07:25,111
What do you think of that ?

114
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:26,863
I think you 're a louse .

115
00:07:26,905 --> 00:07:30,533
I am . Good day , Miss Daniels . Madam .

116
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:34,579
And I 'm glad you didn 't get your lovebirds .

117
00:07:34,663 --> 00:07:38,458
Oh , I 'll find something else . See you in court .

118
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:43,088
Who was that man ?

119
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:45,048
I have no idea .

120
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:06,987
( INAUDIBLE )

121
00:08:11,116 --> 00:08:14,119
They said the mynah bird would be here later this afternoon ,

122
00:08:14,202 --> 00:08:15,662
if you care to come back .

123
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:16,830
No , you 'd better send him .

124
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:17,914
May I use this phone ?

125
00:08:17,998 --> 00:08:19,916
Why , certainly .

126
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:32,095
Daily News ? It 's Melanie Daniels .

127
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:33,596
Could you get me the City Desk , please ?

128
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:35,890
Just a minute , Mrs. MacGruder .

129
00:08:36,891 --> 00:08:39,102
Hello , Charlie . Melanie .

130
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:41,938
I want you to do a favor for me .

131
00:08:42,022 --> 00:08:45,108
No , this is a small one .

132
00:08:45,191 --> 00:08:49,863
Pressure you ? Why , Charlie , darling , would I try to pressure you ?

133
00:08:50,113 --> 00:08:52,741
Would you call the Department of Motor Vehicles for me ?

134
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:55,076
Find out who owns this license plate ,

135
00:08:55,118 --> 00:08:58,413
W-J-H-0-0-3 .

136
00:08:58,455 --> 00:09:00,081
Yes , a California plate .

137
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:04,210
No . I 'll stop off in a little while . Is Daddy in his office ?

138
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:09,799
No , I don 't want to break in on a meeting . Tell him I 'll see him later .

139
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:12,719
Thank you , Charlie .

140
00:09:17,348 --> 00:09:18,725
Do you have any lovebirds ?

141
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:23,605
Well , no , not in the shop , but I can order them for you .

142
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:24,689
How soon ?

143
00:09:24,773 --> 00:09:26,775
Well , when would you want them ?

144
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:27,984
Immediately .

145
00:09:28,068 --> 00:09:30,445
Well , I could probably have them here by tomorrow morning .

146
00:09:30,487 --> 00:09:31,988
Would that be all right ?

147
00:09:32,072 --> 00:09:34,449
That would be just fine .

148
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:43,166
( CHIRPING )

149
00:10:24,916 --> 00:10:27,085
Miss , is that for Mitch Brenner ?

150
00:10:27,168 --> 00:10:28,211
Yes .

151
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,420
He 's not home .

152
00:10:29,504 --> 00:10:30,547
That 's all right .

153
00:10:30,588 --> 00:10:33,758
He won 't be back until Monday , I mean , if those birds are for him .

154
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:35,510
- Monday ? - Yes .

155
00:10:35,844 --> 00:10:37,929
I don 't think you should leave them in the hall , do you ?

156
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:40,056
Well ... Where did he go ?

157
00:10:40,098 --> 00:10:42,308
Bodega Bay . He goes there every weekend .

158
00:10:43,268 --> 00:10:44,394
Bodega Bay . Where 's that ?

159
00:10:44,477 --> 00:10:46,813
Up the coast , about 60 miles north of here .

160
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:49,065
Sixty ...

161
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:51,359
It 's an hour and a half by freeway ,

162
00:10:51,401 --> 00:10:53,153
or two hours if you take the Coast Highway .

163
00:10:53,236 --> 00:10:54,571
Oh .

164
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:57,198
I 'd look after them myself , but I 'm going away , too .

165
00:10:57,824 --> 00:10:59,409
I 'm awfully sorry .

166
00:11:07,876 --> 00:11:09,752
( TIRES SCREECHING )

167
00:12:40,218 --> 00:12:41,636
( BELL DINGS )

168
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:51,354
- Good morning . - Good morning .

169
00:12:51,396 --> 00:12:52,814
I wonder if you could help me .

170
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:53,898
I 'll try my best .

171
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:56,818
I 'm looking for a man named Mitchell Brenner .

172
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,736
- Do you know him ? - Yeah .

173
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,905
- Where does he live ? - Right here , Bodega Bay .

174
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:02,615
Yes , I know , but where ?

175
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:04,409
Right across the bay there .

176
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:06,369
Where ?

177
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:20,675
Now , see where I 'm pointing ?

178
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:21,718
Yes .

179
00:13:21,801 --> 00:13:24,053
See them two big trees across there ?

180
00:13:24,137 --> 00:13:26,014
On the other side of the bay ? Yes .

181
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,682
- And the white house ? - Yes .

182
00:13:27,724 --> 00:13:29,100
That 's where the Brenners live .

183
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:32,020
The Brenners ? Mr. and Mrs. Brenner ?

184
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:34,397
No . Just Lydia and the two kids .

185
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,606
The two kids ?

186
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:37,900
Yeah , Mitch and the little girl .

187
00:13:37,942 --> 00:13:40,653
Oh , I see . How do I get down there ?

188
00:13:40,737 --> 00:13:43,156
You follow the road around the bay ,

189
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:45,241
and that 'll take you right to their front door .

190
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:48,369
The front door . Is there a back road I can take ?

191
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:50,371
No . That 's the only road .

192
00:13:50,413 --> 00:13:52,081
You see , I want to surprise them .

193
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:53,791
Oh .

194
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,626
I don 't want them to see me arrive .

195
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:56,794
Oh .

196
00:13:56,878 --> 00:13:58,504
It 's a surprise , you see .

197
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:01,799
Well , you could get yourself a boat

198
00:14:01,883 --> 00:14:04,635
and cut right across the bay to their dock .

199
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:06,054
Where would I get a boat ?

200
00:14:07,555 --> 00:14:10,141
Down by the Tides Restaurant .

201
00:14:10,850 --> 00:14:12,602
Did you ever handle an outboard boat ?

202
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:13,728
Of course .

203
00:14:15,438 --> 00:14:16,773
Want me to order one for you ?

204
00:14:16,856 --> 00:14:19,150
Well , thank you .

205
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,902
- What name ? - Daniels .

206
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:22,445
Okay .

207
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:23,613
( SHOP BELL DINGS )

208
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:27,950
( DIALING )

209
00:14:35,958 --> 00:14:37,418
I wonder if you could tell me ...

210
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:40,421
Yeah . Just hold it a minute , please .

211
00:14:40,463 --> 00:14:42,048
The little girl 's name ?

212
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:43,591
The little Brenner girl ?

213
00:14:43,633 --> 00:14:44,717
Yes .

214
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:45,968
Alice , I think .

215
00:14:46,761 --> 00:14:49,097
Harry , what 's the little Brenner girl 's name ?

216
00:14:49,639 --> 00:14:51,516
- HARRY : Lois . - SHOPKEEPER : Alice , isn 't it ?

217
00:14:51,724 --> 00:14:52,975
No , it 's Lois .

218
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:54,936
It 's Alice .

219
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:56,771
Are you sure ?

220
00:14:56,813 --> 00:14:59,774
Well , I 'm not positive , if that 's what you mean .

221
00:14:59,816 --> 00:15:01,818
I need her exact name , you see .

222
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:05,321
Oh , just hold on one more minute , please .

223
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:07,824
In that case , I 'll tell you what you do .

224
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:11,202
You go straight through town till you see a little hotel on your left .

225
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:13,413
Then you turn right there .

226
00:15:13,496 --> 00:15:15,164
- Now , you got that ? - Yes .

227
00:15:15,206 --> 00:15:18,167
Near the top of the hill , you 'll see the school , and just beyond ,

228
00:15:18,209 --> 00:15:20,628
a little house with a red mailbox .

229
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:23,506
That 's where Annie Hayworth , the schoolteacher , lives .

230
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,842
You ask her about the little Brenner girl .

231
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:26,968
Well , thank you .

232
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:30,638
Save yourself a lot of trouble . Name 's Alice for sure .

233
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:33,641
Can I have the boat in about 20 minutes ?

234
00:15:33,683 --> 00:15:35,017
How much for the phone calls ?

235
00:15:35,101 --> 00:15:36,561
Oh , it 's nothing .

236
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:37,854
Thank you .

237
00:15:57,999 --> 00:16:00,209
( CHILDREN TALKING INDISTINCTLY )

238
00:16:28,446 --> 00:16:30,072
( DOORBELL RINGS )

239
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:32,742
WOMAN : Who is it ?

240
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:34,243
Me .

241
00:16:34,327 --> 00:16:36,329
Who 's " me " ?

242
00:16:40,583 --> 00:16:42,084
- Miss Hayworth ? - Yes .

243
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:44,420
I 'm Melanie Daniels . I 'm sorry to bother you , but ...

244
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:45,505
Yes ?

245
00:16:45,588 --> 00:16:46,923
The man at the post office sent me .

246
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:49,008
He said you could tell me the name of the little Brenner girl .

247
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:50,092
Cathy ?

248
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:51,844
The one who lives in the white house across the bay ?

249
00:16:51,928 --> 00:16:53,221
That 's the one . Cathy Brenner .

250
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:55,515
He seemed sure it was either Alice or Lois .

251
00:16:55,598 --> 00:16:56,974
Which is why the mail never gets delivered

252
00:16:57,058 --> 00:16:58,809
to the right place in this town .

253
00:16:58,893 --> 00:16:59,894
I 'm sorry . Smoke ?

254
00:16:59,936 --> 00:17:01,103
Thank you .

255
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:07,109
Did you want to see Cathy about something ?

256
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:09,278
Well , not exactly .

257
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:12,365
Oh .

258
00:17:13,783 --> 00:17:16,118
Are you a friend of Mitch 's ?

259
00:17:17,245 --> 00:17:19,163
No , not really .

260
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:23,292
You know , I 've been wanting a cigarette for the last 20 minutes .

261
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:25,628
I just couldn 't convince myself to stop .

262
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:28,089
This tilling of the soil can become compulsive , you know .

263
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,549
It 's a very pretty garden .

264
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:33,177
Oh , thank you . Well , it 's something to do in your spare time .

265
00:17:33,261 --> 00:17:36,514
There 's a lot of spare time in Bodega Bay .

266
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:39,684
Are you planning on staying long ?

267
00:17:39,767 --> 00:17:41,561
No , just a few hours .

268
00:17:41,644 --> 00:17:44,647
Then you 're leaving after you see Cathy ?

269
00:17:44,689 --> 00:17:46,774
Well , something like that .

270
00:17:46,816 --> 00:17:49,110
I 'm sorry . I don 't mean to sound so mysterious .

271
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:51,779
Actually , it 's none of my business .

272
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:54,115
Well , I better be on my way .

273
00:17:55,199 --> 00:17:57,159
- Thank you very much . - Not at all .

274
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,708
Did you drive up from San Francisco by the coast road ?

275
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:05,001
Yes .

276
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:06,294
Nice drive .

277
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:07,503
It 's very beautiful .

278
00:18:08,421 --> 00:18:09,714
Is that where you met Mitch ?

279
00:18:11,632 --> 00:18:12,883
Yes .

280
00:18:15,386 --> 00:18:17,179
I guess that 's where everyone meets Mitch .

281
00:18:17,221 --> 00:18:19,807
Now you sound a bit mysterious , Miss Hayworth .

282
00:18:20,308 --> 00:18:21,350
( CHUCKLES )

283
00:18:21,392 --> 00:18:22,893
Do I ?

284
00:18:22,977 --> 00:18:26,147
I don 't mean to . Actually , I 'm an open book , I 'm afraid .

285
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:27,189
( CHIRPING )

286
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:28,983
Or , rather , a closed one .

287
00:18:30,776 --> 00:18:32,862
Oh , pretty . What are they ?

288
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:34,071
Lovebirds .

289
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:38,868
I see . Good luck , Miss Daniels .

290
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:43,164
Thank you . Can I get out this way ?

291
00:18:44,332 --> 00:18:46,208
Go right around . It 'll take you back to the main road .

292
00:18:46,250 --> 00:18:47,585
Thank you .

293
00:19:15,029 --> 00:19:16,572
( STARTS ENGINE )

294
00:19:40,096 --> 00:19:41,722
( SEAGULLS CAWING )

295
00:20:07,498 --> 00:20:08,916
Do you have a boat for Miss Daniels ?

296
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:10,459
Yes , ma 'am .

297
00:20:10,501 --> 00:20:12,795
It 's the one right below .

298
00:20:15,923 --> 00:20:17,883
( CHIRPING )

299
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:34,859
( MOTOR STARTS )

300
00:21:12,688 --> 00:21:14,148
( MOTOR STOPS )

301
00:24:13,702 --> 00:24:15,537
( MOTOR CRANKING )

302
00:24:26,090 --> 00:24:27,883
( MOTOR STARTS )

303
00:25:43,083 --> 00:25:44,835
- Are you all right ? - Yes , I think so .

304
00:25:45,544 --> 00:25:47,212
What do you suppose made it do that ?

305
00:25:47,296 --> 00:25:48,505
That 's the damnedest thing I ever saw .

306
00:25:48,589 --> 00:25:50,924
I don 't know . It seemed to swoop down at you deliberately .

307
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,009
Oh , you 're bleeding , too .

308
00:25:52,092 --> 00:25:55,012
Let 's take care of that . Okay ?

309
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:56,680
That 's a girl .

310
00:26:03,771 --> 00:26:05,189
Come on .

311
00:26:08,317 --> 00:26:10,527
What happened , Mitch ?

312
00:26:10,611 --> 00:26:12,362
- Gull hit her . - A gull ?

313
00:26:16,867 --> 00:26:18,827
Let 's try up at the restaurant , all right ?

314
00:26:21,872 --> 00:26:23,248
Might need a tetanus shot .

315
00:26:23,332 --> 00:26:26,460
I had a booster before I went abroad last May .

316
00:26:40,057 --> 00:26:42,267
( PEOPLE TALKING INDISTINCTLY )

317
00:26:53,695 --> 00:26:54,696
What happened ?

318
00:26:54,780 --> 00:26:56,740
Hello , Deke . Young lady cut herself .

319
00:26:56,824 --> 00:26:58,075
Shall I call a doctor ?

320
00:26:58,158 --> 00:27:00,869
No , I don 't think it 's that serious . Let 's see .

321
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:03,539
Helen , get some cotton and antiseptic .

322
00:27:04,665 --> 00:27:07,543
You cut yourself outside , miss ?

323
00:27:07,584 --> 00:27:10,045
Don 't worry , Deke . She did it in a boat .

324
00:27:10,087 --> 00:27:12,089
Well , I had a man trip and fall in the parking lot once .

325
00:27:12,172 --> 00:27:13,590
Sued me before I could bat an eyelash .

326
00:27:13,674 --> 00:27:15,050
I don 't think Miss Daniels is gonna sue anybody .

327
00:27:15,134 --> 00:27:16,760
Here .

328
00:27:16,844 --> 00:27:18,303
Well , you 're the lawyer .

329
00:27:18,387 --> 00:27:19,388
Thank you .

330
00:27:20,889 --> 00:27:21,890
What 's that ?

331
00:27:21,974 --> 00:27:23,350
Just some peroxide .

332
00:27:23,392 --> 00:27:25,644
I 'll clean out the cut .

333
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:30,232
So you 're a lawyer .

334
00:27:30,274 --> 00:27:31,441
That 's right .

335
00:27:31,525 --> 00:27:33,443
Of course , I usually defend people , Miss Daniels ,

336
00:27:33,527 --> 00:27:34,862
but if I were prosecuting ...

337
00:27:34,903 --> 00:27:35,946
Do you practice here ?

338
00:27:36,029 --> 00:27:38,699
Uh-uh . San Francisco . What are you doing up here ?

339
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:40,075
What kind of law ?

340
00:27:40,159 --> 00:27:41,451
Criminal .

341
00:27:41,535 --> 00:27:43,912
Is that why you want to see everyone behind bars ?

342
00:27:43,954 --> 00:27:45,581
Oh , not everyone , Miss Daniels .

343
00:27:45,622 --> 00:27:47,749
Only violators and practical jokers .

344
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:49,251
That 's right .

345
00:27:49,293 --> 00:27:50,711
- Ow ! - Oh , sorry .

346
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:53,255
What are you doing up here ?

347
00:27:53,297 --> 00:27:55,632
Didn 't you see the lovebirds ?

348
00:27:57,342 --> 00:28:00,262
Oh , you mean , you came all this way to bring me those birds ?

349
00:28:01,054 --> 00:28:02,389
To bring your sister those birds .

350
00:28:02,431 --> 00:28:04,099
You said it was her birthday .

351
00:28:04,141 --> 00:28:05,601
Besides , I was coming up anyway .

352
00:28:06,935 --> 00:28:08,187
What for ?

353
00:28:09,271 --> 00:28:11,398
To see a friend of mine . Careful .

354
00:28:11,440 --> 00:28:15,485
Oh , sorry . Who 's your friend ?

355
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:19,364
Annie Hayworth , the schoolteacher .

356
00:28:19,448 --> 00:28:20,991
Annie Hayworth .

357
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:24,328
Well , small world .

358
00:28:25,287 --> 00:28:26,371
Yes .

359
00:28:28,123 --> 00:28:30,292
How do you know Annie ?

360
00:28:30,334 --> 00:28:34,338
We went to school together , college .

361
00:28:34,421 --> 00:28:38,967
Did you ? Imagine that . How long are you staying up here ?

362
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:41,637
The weekend .

363
00:28:43,222 --> 00:28:46,808
Well , I think the bleeding 's almost stopped . Why don 't you hold that on ?

364
00:28:55,901 --> 00:28:57,152
So you came up to see Annie , huh ?

365
00:28:57,236 --> 00:28:59,112
Yes .

366
00:28:59,154 --> 00:29:00,364
I think you came up to see me .

367
00:29:00,447 --> 00:29:03,200
Now , why would I want to see you of all people ?

368
00:29:03,283 --> 00:29:05,953
I don 't know , but you must 've gone to a lot of trouble

369
00:29:05,994 --> 00:29:08,038
to find out who I was and where I lived .

370
00:29:08,121 --> 00:29:11,041
It was no trouble at all . I simply called my father 's newspaper .

371
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:14,836
Besides , I was coming up anyway . I 've already told you that .

372
00:29:14,878 --> 00:29:16,004
You really like me , huh ?

373
00:29:16,046 --> 00:29:17,839
I loathe you .

374
00:29:18,632 --> 00:29:21,551
You have no manners . You 're arrogant , and conceited , and ...

375
00:29:21,635 --> 00:29:24,846
I wrote you a letter about it , in fact , but I tore it up .

376
00:29:24,888 --> 00:29:26,014
What did it say ?

377
00:29:26,056 --> 00:29:28,058
None of your business .

378
00:29:29,142 --> 00:29:31,019
I can 't say I like your seagulls much , either .

379
00:29:31,061 --> 00:29:32,145
I come all the way up here to ...

380
00:29:32,187 --> 00:29:33,689
But you were coming up anyway , remember ?

381
00:29:38,902 --> 00:29:40,237
Mitch ?

382
00:29:41,071 --> 00:29:43,407
I thought I saw your car . What are you doing in town ?

383
00:29:43,490 --> 00:29:44,908
I had to acknowledge a delivery .

384
00:29:44,992 --> 00:29:46,076
Of what ?

385
00:29:46,159 --> 00:29:49,246
Mother , I 'd like you to meet Melanie Daniels . Miss Daniels , my mother .

386
00:29:49,329 --> 00:29:50,706
How do you do ?

387
00:29:51,999 --> 00:29:55,168
How do you do , Miss Daniels ? Acknowledge a what ?

388
00:29:55,210 --> 00:29:58,588
A delivery . Miss Daniels brought us some birds from San Francisco .

389
00:29:58,672 --> 00:30:01,258
For Cathy for her birthday . Where is she ?

390
00:30:01,341 --> 00:30:02,884
Across at Brinkmeyer 's .

391
00:30:02,926 --> 00:30:05,220
As a matter of fact , Miss Daniels is staying up here for the weekend ,

392
00:30:05,304 --> 00:30:07,889
so I 've already invited her for dinner tonight .

393
00:30:11,768 --> 00:30:14,021
Well , you did go to the trouble of bringing those birds .

394
00:30:14,062 --> 00:30:15,731
MELANIE : Oh , I couldn 't possibly .

395
00:30:15,772 --> 00:30:17,399
You did say birds ?

396
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:19,776
Yes , lovebirds .

397
00:30:20,527 --> 00:30:21,862
Oh , I see .

398
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:27,451
MITCH : So we couldn 't let you get away

399
00:30:27,534 --> 00:30:28,994
without thanking you in some small way .

400
00:30:29,077 --> 00:30:31,288
And you haven 't met Cathy , and you are staying the weekend .

401
00:30:31,371 --> 00:30:32,456
Well , yes , but ...

402
00:30:32,539 --> 00:30:33,790
Well , you are , aren 't you ?

403
00:30:33,874 --> 00:30:35,000
Certainly , but ...

404
00:30:35,083 --> 00:30:36,126
MITCH : Then it 's all settled .

405
00:30:36,209 --> 00:30:37,878
What time is dinner , Mother ?

406
00:30:37,919 --> 00:30:39,379
7 : 00 , the same as usual .

407
00:30:39,421 --> 00:30:41,048
I 'll pick you up . Where are you staying ?

408
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:42,382
With Annie , of course .

409
00:30:43,258 --> 00:30:46,470
Oh , of course . How stupid of me . 6 : 45 ?

410
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:49,306
Annie may have made other plans . I 'll have to see .

411
00:30:50,098 --> 00:30:51,933
Besides , I can find my own way .

412
00:30:51,975 --> 00:30:53,769
You 're sure now ? You won 't hire a boat or anything ?

413
00:30:54,478 --> 00:30:55,562
I 'm sure .

414
00:30:55,604 --> 00:30:56,605
MITCH : 7 : 00 , then .

415
00:30:57,439 --> 00:30:58,440
Maybe .

416
00:30:59,483 --> 00:31:01,818
We 'll be waiting for you . How 's your head ?

417
00:31:01,902 --> 00:31:03,904
Much better , thank you .

418
00:31:03,945 --> 00:31:07,032
A gull hit me , Mrs. Brenner , that 's all .

419
00:31:13,121 --> 00:31:14,414
( RINGING )

420
00:31:20,545 --> 00:31:22,631
Oh , hi . Did you find her all right ?

421
00:31:22,672 --> 00:31:24,257
Yes , I did .

422
00:31:24,299 --> 00:31:26,551
I was wondering ...

423
00:31:26,635 --> 00:31:28,053
That sign there .

424
00:31:30,305 --> 00:31:33,141
Do you suppose I could have the room for just a single night ?

425
00:31:33,183 --> 00:31:35,102
I was planning on renting it for a longer time ...

426
00:31:35,143 --> 00:31:36,186
I would appreciate it .

427
00:31:36,269 --> 00:31:38,313
I 've tried everywhere in town . They 're all full .

428
00:31:39,648 --> 00:31:42,818
Well , all right . Got your bags in the car ?

429
00:31:44,111 --> 00:31:47,155
( CHUCKLES ) Well , it 's utilitarian , I 'll say that .

430
00:31:47,197 --> 00:31:50,158
I just picked up some things for the night at the general store .

431
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:51,993
You see , I hadn 't planned on staying very long .

432
00:31:53,328 --> 00:31:57,124
Yes , I know . Did something unexpected come up ?

433
00:31:58,708 --> 00:32:02,045
Yes . May I use your phone ? I 'd like to call home .

434
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:05,340
I just put some coffee on the stove .

435
00:32:05,424 --> 00:32:07,217
( SEAGULLS CAWING )

436
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:09,594
Don 't they ever stop migrating ?

437
00:32:09,678 --> 00:32:11,012
( CAWING )

438
00:32:53,221 --> 00:32:54,222
( RINGS )

439
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:06,902
Hi !

440
00:33:08,862 --> 00:33:10,155
Hi !

441
00:33:11,448 --> 00:33:12,532
Miss Daniels ?

442
00:33:12,574 --> 00:33:13,658
Yes .

443
00:33:14,993 --> 00:33:17,162
Oh , they 're beautiful !

444
00:33:17,245 --> 00:33:20,207
They 're just what I wanted . Is there a man and a woman ?

445
00:33:21,082 --> 00:33:22,834
I can 't tell which is which .

446
00:33:22,918 --> 00:33:24,252
MELANIE : Well , I suppose so .

447
00:33:24,336 --> 00:33:25,837
MITCH : Hello there . Annie had no plans , huh ?

448
00:33:25,921 --> 00:33:26,922
MELANIE : No .

449
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:28,924
Fine . We 're very glad you could come . You hungry ?

450
00:33:29,007 --> 00:33:31,259
- Reasonably . - Dinner 's just about ready .

451
00:33:31,343 --> 00:33:32,427
We 've been out back looking at the chickens .

452
00:33:32,469 --> 00:33:33,678
Something seems to be wrong with them .

453
00:33:33,762 --> 00:33:35,722
There 's nothing wrong with those chickens , Mitch .

454
00:33:35,764 --> 00:33:37,349
I 'm going to call Fred Brinkmeyer right now .

455
00:33:37,432 --> 00:33:38,433
What good 's that gonna do ?

456
00:33:38,517 --> 00:33:40,435
The chickens won 't eat .

457
00:33:40,519 --> 00:33:42,896
He sold the feed to me , didn 't he ?

458
00:33:42,938 --> 00:33:44,981
Caveat emptor , Mother . " Let the buyer beware . "

459
00:33:45,065 --> 00:33:46,608
Whose side are you on ?

460
00:33:46,650 --> 00:33:48,193
Merely quoting the law , dear .

461
00:33:48,276 --> 00:33:49,945
Never mind the law .

462
00:33:57,285 --> 00:34:01,373
This won 't take long , Miss ... Hello , Fred ? Lydia Brenner .

463
00:34:01,456 --> 00:34:03,250
- I didn 't interrupt your dinner , did I ? - How about a drink ?

464
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:04,334
Thank you , I 'd love one .

465
00:34:04,417 --> 00:34:07,629
Fred , that feed you sold me is no good .

466
00:34:07,712 --> 00:34:09,506
The chicken feed .

467
00:34:09,589 --> 00:34:12,968
Well , it 's just no good . The chickens won 't eat it .

468
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:15,303
They 're always hungry .

469
00:34:15,387 --> 00:34:16,805
I opened a sack for them when I got home ,

470
00:34:16,888 --> 00:34:18,223
and they just wouldn 't touch it .

471
00:34:18,390 --> 00:34:20,600
You know chickens as well as I do , and when they won 't eat ,

472
00:34:20,642 --> 00:34:23,937
there 's something wrong with what they 're being fed . That 's all .

473
00:34:23,979 --> 00:34:26,648
No , they 're not fussy chickens .

474
00:34:27,983 --> 00:34:31,152
Who ? What 's he got to do with it ?

475
00:34:31,236 --> 00:34:32,445
Is that your father ?

476
00:34:32,487 --> 00:34:33,989
Mmm-hmm . Please sit down .

477
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:36,992
Fred , I don 't care how many sacks of feed you sold him .

478
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:38,326
My chicken ...

479
00:34:40,120 --> 00:34:41,997
Oh , I see .

480
00:34:43,331 --> 00:34:45,083
Dan Fawcett .

481
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:46,835
This afternoon ?

482
00:34:46,876 --> 00:34:49,921
Well , that just proves what I 'm saying ! The feed you sold us ...

483
00:34:52,132 --> 00:34:53,174
Oh .

484
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:58,972
Well , maybe I 'd better go over and see him .

485
00:34:59,014 --> 00:35:01,891
You don 't think there 's something going around , do you ?

486
00:35:02,934 --> 00:35:04,352
No , never !

487
00:35:05,437 --> 00:35:09,024
No , Fred , they don 't seem sick at all . They just won 't eat .

488
00:35:10,025 --> 00:35:11,192
Uh-huh .

489
00:35:13,278 --> 00:35:17,032
Well , I 'll try to go over and see him . Maybe he ...

490
00:35:17,991 --> 00:35:19,200
Uh-huh .

491
00:35:19,701 --> 00:35:21,745
All right . Thanks .

492
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:28,168
He had a call from Dan Fawcett a while ago .

493
00:35:28,209 --> 00:35:30,170
His chickens won 't eat either .

494
00:35:30,211 --> 00:35:33,673
It 's what you said , Mom . Mr. Brinkmeyer 's feed is no good .

495
00:35:33,715 --> 00:35:37,385
No , Cathy . He sold Mr. Fawcett a different brand .

496
00:35:37,469 --> 00:35:40,221
You don 't think they 're getting sick , do you , Mitch ?

497
00:35:46,853 --> 00:35:49,773
I still don 't understand how you knew I wanted lovebirds .

498
00:35:49,856 --> 00:35:51,691
Your brother told me .

499
00:35:51,733 --> 00:35:55,570
Then you knew Mitch in San Francisco ? Is that right ?

500
00:35:55,654 --> 00:35:57,697
No , not exactly .

501
00:35:57,739 --> 00:36:00,659
Mitch knows a lot of people in San Francisco .

502
00:36:00,742 --> 00:36:02,577
Of course , they 're mostly hoods .

503
00:36:03,078 --> 00:36:04,245
Cathy !

504
00:36:04,287 --> 00:36:06,581
Well , Mom , he 's the first to admit it .

505
00:36:06,665 --> 00:36:10,377
He spends half his day in the detention cells at the Hall of Justice .

506
00:36:10,418 --> 00:36:13,755
In a democracy , Cathy , everyone is entitled to a fair trial .

507
00:36:13,797 --> 00:36:15,048
Your brother 's practice ...

508
00:36:15,090 --> 00:36:16,591
Oh , Mom , please !

509
00:36:16,633 --> 00:36:19,844
I know all that democracy jazz . They 're still hoods .

510
00:36:22,472 --> 00:36:26,142
He has a client now who shot his wife in the head six times .

511
00:36:26,226 --> 00:36:29,312
Six times ! Can you imagine it ?

512
00:36:29,396 --> 00:36:33,441
I mean , even twice would be overdoing it , don 't you think ?

513
00:36:34,150 --> 00:36:35,151
Why did he shoot her ?

514
00:36:35,235 --> 00:36:37,028
He was watching a ball game on television .

515
00:36:37,112 --> 00:36:38,279
What ?

516
00:36:38,321 --> 00:36:40,115
His wife changed the channel .

517
00:36:42,117 --> 00:36:44,244
Are you coming to my party tomorrow ?

518
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:45,578
I don 't think so .

519
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:48,081
I have to get back to San Francisco .

520
00:36:49,165 --> 00:36:50,166
Don 't you like us ?

521
00:36:50,250 --> 00:36:52,627
Oh , darling , of course I do .

522
00:36:52,711 --> 00:36:54,295
Don 't you like Bodega Bay ?

523
00:36:54,379 --> 00:36:55,547
I don 't know yet .

524
00:36:55,630 --> 00:36:59,134
Mitch likes it very much . He comes up every weekend , you know ,

525
00:36:59,217 --> 00:37:02,137
even though he has his own apartment in the city .

526
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:05,598
He says San Francisco 's like an anthill at the foot of a bridge .

527
00:37:05,640 --> 00:37:08,143
I suppose it does get a little hectic at times .

528
00:37:08,893 --> 00:37:12,522
Well , if you do decide to come , don 't say I told you about it .

529
00:37:12,605 --> 00:37:14,816
It 's supposed to be a surprise party .

530
00:37:14,858 --> 00:37:17,986
You see , they 've got this whole complicated thing figured out ,

531
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:20,488
where I 'm going over to Michele 's for the afternoon ,

532
00:37:20,572 --> 00:37:22,490
and Michele 's mother will say that she has a headache .

533
00:37:22,574 --> 00:37:24,659
Would I mind very much if she took me home ?

534
00:37:24,743 --> 00:37:27,787
Then when I get home here , all the kids will jump out !

535
00:37:30,665 --> 00:37:33,793
Oh , won 't you come ? Won 't you please come ?

536
00:37:36,629 --> 00:37:38,590
I don 't think so .

537
00:37:40,842 --> 00:37:42,677
She 's a charming girl , isn 't she , Mitch ?

538
00:37:42,761 --> 00:37:44,387
MITCH : Hmm ? Yes .

539
00:37:44,471 --> 00:37:45,638
Certainly pretty .

540
00:37:45,680 --> 00:37:46,848
Mmm-hmm .

541
00:37:46,890 --> 00:37:48,099
How long have you known her ?

542
00:37:48,183 --> 00:37:50,935
Now , I told you , dear , we met yesterday .

543
00:37:51,019 --> 00:37:52,145
In a bird shop .

544
00:37:52,187 --> 00:37:53,188
In a bird shop .

545
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:55,190
She was selling birds ?

546
00:37:55,690 --> 00:37:59,527
No , no . I just led her into believing that I believed she was , and then ...

547
00:37:59,569 --> 00:38:00,779
Well , it 's all very complicated .

548
00:38:00,862 --> 00:38:02,197
But she did buy the lovebirds ,

549
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:03,865
and then drove all the way out here .

550
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:05,492
- Mother . - Yes ?

551
00:38:05,533 --> 00:38:07,285
Where did you go to law school ?

552
00:38:09,412 --> 00:38:10,914
Forgive me .

553
00:38:10,997 --> 00:38:14,542
I suppose I 'm just naturally curious about a girl like that .

554
00:38:15,210 --> 00:38:16,461
She 's very rich , isn 't she ?

555
00:38:16,544 --> 00:38:17,796
Yeah , I suppose so .

556
00:38:17,879 --> 00:38:20,131
Her father 's part owner of one of the big newspapers in San Francisco .

557
00:38:20,215 --> 00:38:23,384
You 'd think he could manage to keep her name out of print .

558
00:38:23,426 --> 00:38:25,553
She 's always mentioned in the columns , Mitch .

559
00:38:25,595 --> 00:38:27,388
Yes , I know .

560
00:38:27,430 --> 00:38:30,934
She is the one who jumped into a fountain in Rome last summer , isn 't she ?

561
00:38:32,393 --> 00:38:33,603
Yes .

562
00:38:34,395 --> 00:38:35,897
I supposed I 'm old-fashioned .

563
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:38,983
I know it was supposed to be very warm there , but ...

564
00:38:39,067 --> 00:38:41,569
Well , actually , the newspapers said she was naked .

565
00:38:41,653 --> 00:38:43,571
Yes , I know , dear .

566
00:38:43,613 --> 00:38:45,073
Of course , it 's none of my business ,

567
00:38:45,114 --> 00:38:46,449
but when you bring a girl like that ...

568
00:38:46,533 --> 00:38:47,742
Darling ?

569
00:38:47,784 --> 00:38:48,785
Yes ?

570
00:38:48,868 --> 00:38:52,580
I think I can handle Melanie Daniels by myself .

571
00:38:52,622 --> 00:38:56,584
Well , as long as you know what you want , Mitch .

572
00:38:58,002 --> 00:39:00,588
I know exactly what I want .

573
00:39:05,885 --> 00:39:07,345
Be able to find your way back all right ?

574
00:39:07,428 --> 00:39:09,305
Oh , yes .

575
00:39:11,474 --> 00:39:12,725
Will I be seeing you again ?

576
00:39:12,767 --> 00:39:14,936
San Francisco 's a long way from here .

577
00:39:14,978 --> 00:39:16,563
I 'm in San Francisco five days a week

578
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:17,647
with a lot of time on my hands .

579
00:39:17,730 --> 00:39:18,731
I 'd like to see you .

580
00:39:19,566 --> 00:39:21,276
Maybe we could go swimming or something .

581
00:39:21,359 --> 00:39:22,944
Mother tells me you like to swim .

582
00:39:23,945 --> 00:39:25,572
How does Mother know what I like to do ?

583
00:39:25,613 --> 00:39:27,782
I guess we read the same gossip column .

584
00:39:27,824 --> 00:39:30,201
Oh , that . Rome .

585
00:39:30,285 --> 00:39:32,120
Yeah , I really like to swim . I think we might get along very well .

586
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:34,539
In case you 're interested , I was pushed into that fountain .

587
00:39:34,622 --> 00:39:35,874
Without any clothes on ?

588
00:39:35,957 --> 00:39:38,877
With all my clothes on . The newspaper that ran that story

589
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:40,628
happens to be a rival of my father 's paper .

590
00:39:40,670 --> 00:39:42,714
You were just a poor , innocent victim of circumstances ?

591
00:39:42,797 --> 00:39:44,549
I 'm neither poor nor innocent ,

592
00:39:44,632 --> 00:39:45,758
but the truth of that particular ...

593
00:39:45,800 --> 00:39:48,219
The truth is , you 're running around with a pretty wild crowd , isn 't it ?

594
00:39:48,303 --> 00:39:50,138
Yes , that 's the truth , but I was pushed into that fountain ,

595
00:39:50,221 --> 00:39:51,389
and that 's the truth , too .

596
00:39:51,472 --> 00:39:52,724
Uh-huh .

597
00:39:52,807 --> 00:39:54,851
Do you really know Annie Hayworth ?

598
00:39:54,934 --> 00:39:57,437
No . At least I didn 't until I came up here .

599
00:39:57,478 --> 00:39:59,439
- So you didn 't go to school together ? - No .

600
00:39:59,480 --> 00:40:00,982
- And you didn 't come up here to see her ? - No !

601
00:40:01,024 --> 00:40:02,483
- You were lying ! - Yes , I was lying .

602
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:05,153
What about the letter you wrote me ? Is that a lie , too ?

603
00:40:05,194 --> 00:40:06,237
No , I wrote the letter .

604
00:40:07,155 --> 00:40:08,281
Well , what did it say ?

605
00:40:08,323 --> 00:40:09,574
It said , " Dear Mr. Brenner .

606
00:40:09,657 --> 00:40:11,743
" I think you need these lovebirds after all .

607
00:40:11,826 --> 00:40:13,328
" They may help your personality . "

608
00:40:13,411 --> 00:40:15,496
- That 's what it said . - But you tore it up ?

609
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:16,789
- Yes . - Why ?

610
00:40:17,498 --> 00:40:19,709
Because it seemed stupid and foolish .

611
00:40:19,792 --> 00:40:21,169
Like jumping into a fountain in Rome .

612
00:40:21,252 --> 00:40:22,337
I told you what happened !

613
00:40:22,378 --> 00:40:23,504
You don 't expect me to believe that , do you ?

614
00:40:23,546 --> 00:40:25,590
Oh , I don 't give a damn what you believe !

615
00:40:26,424 --> 00:40:28,176
- I 'd still like to see you . - Why ?

616
00:40:28,217 --> 00:40:29,719
I think it might be fun .

617
00:40:29,802 --> 00:40:33,181
That might 've been good enough in Rome , but it 's not good enough now .

618
00:40:33,264 --> 00:40:34,807
- It is for me . - Well , not for me .

619
00:40:34,849 --> 00:40:35,975
What do you want ?

620
00:40:36,017 --> 00:40:37,226
I thought you knew .

621
00:40:37,310 --> 00:40:41,773
I want to go through life jumping into fountains naked . Good night .

622
00:40:51,699 --> 00:40:52,742
( BIRDS SQUAWKING )

623
00:40:53,493 --> 00:40:54,911
( CHIRPING )

624
00:41:02,919 --> 00:41:04,504
Miss Daniels , is that you ?

625
00:41:04,545 --> 00:41:05,713
Yes .

626
00:41:05,755 --> 00:41:06,965
Hi .

627
00:41:08,049 --> 00:41:11,511
Is something wrong ? Is that cut beginning to bother you ?

628
00:41:11,552 --> 00:41:13,846
No , it 's not the cut that 's bothering me .

629
00:41:15,348 --> 00:41:16,432
Would you like some brandy ?

630
00:41:17,725 --> 00:41:19,227
If you have some , I 'd love it .

631
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:21,771
I 'll get it . Why don 't you sit down , Miss Daniels ?

632
00:41:21,854 --> 00:41:24,899
Oh , would you like a sweater or something , a quilt ?

633
00:41:24,983 --> 00:41:27,235
No . No , thank you .

634
00:41:30,697 --> 00:41:31,906
Won 't you call me Melanie ?

635
00:41:31,948 --> 00:41:33,157
All right .

636
00:41:41,541 --> 00:41:42,834
Thank you .

637
00:41:42,917 --> 00:41:44,794
Gets a bit chilly here at night sometimes ,

638
00:41:44,877 --> 00:41:47,130
especially if you 're over near the bay .

639
00:41:49,257 --> 00:41:51,426
Well , how did your evening go ?

640
00:41:53,011 --> 00:41:55,263
Did you meet Lydia ?

641
00:41:56,389 --> 00:41:58,266
Or would you rather I changed the subject ?

642
00:41:58,891 --> 00:42:00,393
I think so .

643
00:42:02,270 --> 00:42:04,272
Well , how do you like our little hamlet ?

644
00:42:05,273 --> 00:42:06,899
I despise it .

645
00:42:06,941 --> 00:42:08,234
( CHUCKLES )

646
00:42:08,276 --> 00:42:11,237
Well , I suppose it doesn 't offer much to the casual visitor ,

647
00:42:11,279 --> 00:42:14,282
unless you 're thrilled by a collection of shacks on a hillside .

648
00:42:14,365 --> 00:42:16,576
It takes a bit of getting used to .

649
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:18,202
Where are you from originally , Annie ?

650
00:42:18,286 --> 00:42:19,537
San Francisco .

651
00:42:19,620 --> 00:42:21,748
How did you happen to come up here ?

652
00:42:24,167 --> 00:42:28,796
A friend invited me up for a weekend a long time ago .

653
00:42:30,631 --> 00:42:32,717
Look , I see no reason for being coy about this .

654
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:34,802
It was Mitch Brenner . I guess you knew that anyway .

655
00:42:34,886 --> 00:42:36,471
I suspected as much .

656
00:42:38,139 --> 00:42:39,766
Well , you needn 't worry .

657
00:42:39,807 --> 00:42:41,934
It 's been over and done with a long time ago .

658
00:42:42,602 --> 00:42:45,313
Annie , there 's nothing between Mr. Brenner and me .

659
00:42:45,396 --> 00:42:46,856
Isn 't there ?

660
00:42:48,024 --> 00:42:49,609
Well , maybe there isn 't .

661
00:42:49,650 --> 00:42:52,320
Maybe there 's never been anything between Mitch and any girl .

662
00:42:53,404 --> 00:42:55,281
What do you mean ?

663
00:42:55,323 --> 00:42:58,451
I think I 'll have some of that .

664
00:42:58,493 --> 00:43:01,287
I was seeing a lot of him in San Francisco .

665
00:43:01,329 --> 00:43:03,623
Then one weekend , he invited me up to meet Lydia .

666
00:43:03,664 --> 00:43:05,166
When was this ?

667
00:43:05,208 --> 00:43:08,920
Oh , four years ago , shortly after his father died .

668
00:43:09,545 --> 00:43:12,131
Of course , things may be different now .

669
00:43:12,173 --> 00:43:13,257
Different ?

670
00:43:14,634 --> 00:43:16,052
With Lydia .

671
00:43:16,844 --> 00:43:18,888
Did she seem a trifle distant ?

672
00:43:18,971 --> 00:43:20,181
A trifle .

673
00:43:21,015 --> 00:43:23,518
Well , then perhaps things aren 't quite so different .

674
00:43:24,644 --> 00:43:27,105
You know , her attitude nearly drove me crazy .

675
00:43:27,188 --> 00:43:28,773
When I got back to San Francisco ,

676
00:43:28,856 --> 00:43:31,567
I spent days trying to figure out exactly what I 'd done to displease her .

677
00:43:32,318 --> 00:43:33,361
Well , what had you done ?

678
00:43:34,403 --> 00:43:35,655
Nothing .

679
00:43:35,696 --> 00:43:40,409
I simply existed . So what 's the answer ? A jealous woman , right ?

680
00:43:40,493 --> 00:43:42,453
A clinging , possessive mother ?

681
00:43:42,537 --> 00:43:43,913
Wrong .

682
00:43:43,996 --> 00:43:45,373
With all due respect to Oedipus ,

683
00:43:45,456 --> 00:43:46,541
I don 't think that was the case .

684
00:43:46,624 --> 00:43:48,251
Then what was it ?

685
00:43:50,002 --> 00:43:52,713
Lydia liked me . That 's the strange part .

686
00:43:53,464 --> 00:43:55,716
Now that I 'm no longer a threat , we 're very good friends .

687
00:43:55,800 --> 00:43:57,718
Then why did she object to you ?

688
00:43:59,095 --> 00:44:00,221
Because she was afraid .

689
00:44:00,304 --> 00:44:02,181
Afraid you 'd take Mitch ?

690
00:44:03,099 --> 00:44:04,600
Afraid I 'd give Mitch .

691
00:44:04,809 --> 00:44:06,435
I don 't understand .

692
00:44:06,519 --> 00:44:07,979
Afraid of any woman who would give Mitch

693
00:44:08,062 --> 00:44:10,773
the one thing Lydia can give him , love .

694
00:44:10,857 --> 00:44:13,401
That adds up to a jealous , possessive woman .

695
00:44:14,152 --> 00:44:16,571
No , I don 't think so .

696
00:44:16,612 --> 00:44:19,782
You see , she 's not afraid of losing Mitch .

697
00:44:20,533 --> 00:44:22,160
She 's only afraid of being abandoned .

698
00:44:22,243 --> 00:44:24,579
Someone ought to tell her she 'd be gaining a daughter .

699
00:44:24,662 --> 00:44:25,997
( CHUCKLES )

700
00:44:26,747 --> 00:44:29,709
No . She already has a daughter .

701
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:33,462
Well , what about Mitch ? Didn 't he have anything to say about this ?

702
00:44:34,839 --> 00:44:37,425
Well , I can understand his position .

703
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:40,094
He 'd just been through a lot with Lydia after his father died .

704
00:44:40,178 --> 00:44:42,054
He didn 't want to risk going through it all again .

705
00:44:42,388 --> 00:44:43,764
Oh , I see .

706
00:44:43,806 --> 00:44:46,309
So it ended . Not right then , of course .

707
00:44:46,392 --> 00:44:49,770
We went back to San Francisco , saw each other now and then ,

708
00:44:49,812 --> 00:44:51,314
but we both knew it was over .

709
00:44:51,397 --> 00:44:53,441
Then what are you doing here in Bodega Bay ?

710
00:44:54,483 --> 00:44:55,943
I wanted to be near Mitch .

711
00:44:56,944 --> 00:44:59,614
Oh , it was over and done with , and I knew it , but ...

712
00:44:59,697 --> 00:45:01,699
I still wanted to be near him .

713
00:45:02,408 --> 00:45:04,410
You see , I still like him a hell of a lot ,

714
00:45:05,870 --> 00:45:09,665
and I don 't want to lose that friendship , ever .

715
00:45:09,832 --> 00:45:11,125
( PHONE RINGING )

716
00:45:19,550 --> 00:45:20,635
Hello .

717
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:22,887
Hello .

718
00:45:23,554 --> 00:45:25,598
No , no , no , I wasn 't asleep .

719
00:45:26,766 --> 00:45:28,851
Yes , just a little while ago .

720
00:45:29,936 --> 00:45:31,812
Sure . Hold on .

721
00:45:33,105 --> 00:45:34,190
It 's Mitch .

722
00:45:34,273 --> 00:45:35,650
For you .

723
00:45:43,908 --> 00:45:47,245
Hello ? Oh , yes , this is Melanie .

724
00:45:48,621 --> 00:45:50,706
Fine , thank you .

725
00:45:50,790 --> 00:45:54,502
No , no trouble at all . I simply followed the road .

726
00:45:56,337 --> 00:45:59,423
Well ... there 's no need to apologize .

727
00:45:59,507 --> 00:46:01,133
I can understand .

728
00:46:03,010 --> 00:46:06,180
That 's very kind of you . No , I 'm not angry .

729
00:46:09,725 --> 00:46:13,104
Well , I couldn 't . I have to get back to San Francisco .

730
00:46:15,398 --> 00:46:18,484
No , I wouldn 't want to disappoint Cathy , but ...

731
00:46:22,905 --> 00:46:24,031
I see .

732
00:46:25,866 --> 00:46:28,619
All right . Yes , I 'll be there .

733
00:46:29,453 --> 00:46:30,788
Good night , Mitch .

734
00:46:34,041 --> 00:46:36,419
He wants me to go to Cathy 's party tomorrow afternoon .

735
00:46:36,502 --> 00:46:37,712
I said I would .

736
00:46:38,713 --> 00:46:39,839
It should be fun .

737
00:46:40,548 --> 00:46:42,591
I 'll be there , too , to help .

738
00:46:42,675 --> 00:46:45,594
Oh , it seems so pointless .

739
00:46:45,678 --> 00:46:49,598
Well , I think I 'll go to sleep . It 's been a busy day .

740
00:46:54,895 --> 00:46:56,897
My luggage .

741
00:47:00,401 --> 00:47:03,529
That 's pretty . Where 'd you get that ? Brinkmeyer 's ?

742
00:47:03,571 --> 00:47:04,655
Mmm .

743
00:47:05,573 --> 00:47:07,074
Do you think I should go ?

744
00:47:07,742 --> 00:47:09,327
Well , that 's up to you .

745
00:47:10,161 --> 00:47:11,912
No , it 's really up to Lydia , isn 't it ?

746
00:47:13,831 --> 00:47:16,584
Never mind Lydia . Do you want to go ?

747
00:47:17,835 --> 00:47:18,878
Yes .

748
00:47:19,712 --> 00:47:20,755
Then go .

749
00:47:20,838 --> 00:47:22,423
Thank you , Annie .

750
00:47:22,923 --> 00:47:24,425
( CLATTERING ) Oh .

751
00:47:24,467 --> 00:47:27,345
Wonder who that can be .

752
00:47:27,428 --> 00:47:29,513
Is someone there ?

753
00:47:29,597 --> 00:47:31,849
Who is it ?

754
00:47:31,932 --> 00:47:33,434
Look .

755
00:47:34,894 --> 00:47:38,439
Poor thing . Probably lost his way in the dark .

756
00:47:39,523 --> 00:47:41,525
But it isn 't dark , Annie .

757
00:47:42,276 --> 00:47:44,403
There 's a full moon .

758
00:47:51,577 --> 00:47:53,037
( CHILDREN CHATTERING AND LAUGHING )

759
00:47:53,120 --> 00:47:56,123
ANNIE : Cathy , that 's very good . Very good .

760
00:47:58,292 --> 00:48:00,586
Okay . Here we go .

761
00:48:20,231 --> 00:48:23,734
Attagirl . Come on . Don 't let him get you .

762
00:48:29,115 --> 00:48:30,491
( INAUDIBLE )

763
00:48:40,126 --> 00:48:42,128
No , I really shouldn 't have any more . I 'm driving .

764
00:48:42,169 --> 00:48:44,296
Well , actually , I 'm trying to get you to stay for dinner .

765
00:48:44,338 --> 00:48:45,798
A lot of roast beef left over .

766
00:48:45,840 --> 00:48:49,301
No , I couldn 't possibly . I have to get back .

767
00:48:49,343 --> 00:48:50,845
All right .

768
00:48:50,886 --> 00:48:52,888
- Cheers . - Cheers .

769
00:48:55,182 --> 00:48:56,976
Seriously , why do you have to rush off ?

770
00:48:57,017 --> 00:48:58,727
What 's so important in San Francisco ?

771
00:48:58,811 --> 00:49:02,356
Well , I have to get to work tomorrow morning , for one thing .

772
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:04,108
You have a job ?

773
00:49:04,191 --> 00:49:05,484
I have several jobs .

774
00:49:05,526 --> 00:49:07,153
What do you do ?

775
00:49:07,194 --> 00:49:09,155
I do different things on different days .

776
00:49:09,196 --> 00:49:10,614
Like what ?

777
00:49:10,698 --> 00:49:11,907
Well , on Mondays and Wednesdays ,

778
00:49:11,991 --> 00:49:13,701
I work for the Travelers ' Aid at the airport .

779
00:49:13,742 --> 00:49:14,785
Helping travelers ?

780
00:49:15,911 --> 00:49:19,081
No , misdirecting them . I thought you could read my character .

781
00:49:19,707 --> 00:49:23,252
On Tuesdays , I take a course in General Semantics at Berkeley ,

782
00:49:23,335 --> 00:49:25,421
finding new four-letter words .

783
00:49:25,504 --> 00:49:27,715
That 's not a job , of course ... You mean , you don 't have to ...

784
00:49:27,798 --> 00:49:30,551
And on Thursdays , I have my meeting and lunch .

785
00:49:30,593 --> 00:49:32,303
In the underworld , I suppose .

786
00:49:32,386 --> 00:49:34,555
I shall disappoint you .

787
00:49:34,597 --> 00:49:37,683
We 're sending a little Korean boy through school .

788
00:49:37,725 --> 00:49:40,186
We actually raise money for it .

789
00:49:44,773 --> 00:49:47,109
You see , Rome ...

790
00:49:47,193 --> 00:49:49,737
That entire summer , I did nothing but ...

791
00:49:51,739 --> 00:49:53,657
Well , it was very easy to get lost there .

792
00:49:54,783 --> 00:49:57,411
So when I came back , I thought it was time I began ...

793
00:49:57,453 --> 00:49:59,747
Oh , I don 't know , finding something again .

794
00:50:03,626 --> 00:50:06,879
So , on Mondays and Thursdays , I keep myself busy .

795
00:50:08,130 --> 00:50:09,131
What about Fridays ?

796
00:50:09,215 --> 00:50:10,841
Fridays ? They 're free .

797
00:50:13,469 --> 00:50:17,264
I sometimes go to bird shops on Fridays .

798
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:20,351
I 'm very glad you do .

799
00:50:21,185 --> 00:50:22,436
A nice , innocent , little day .

800
00:50:22,520 --> 00:50:23,938
Oh , yes .

801
00:50:27,483 --> 00:50:30,903
I have an Aunt Tessa . Have you got an Aunt Tessa ?

802
00:50:30,945 --> 00:50:33,906
Mine is very prim and straight-laced .

803
00:50:33,948 --> 00:50:36,909
I 'm giving her a mynah bird when she comes back from Europe .

804
00:50:36,951 --> 00:50:38,619
Mynah birds talk , you know .

805
00:50:39,537 --> 00:50:41,247
Can you see my Aunt Tessa 's face ,

806
00:50:41,288 --> 00:50:45,751
when this one tells us one or two of the words I 've picked up at Berkeley ?

807
00:50:46,377 --> 00:50:48,337
You need a mother 's care , my child .

808
00:50:51,507 --> 00:50:52,800
Not my mother 's .

809
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:55,094
Oh , I 'm sorry .

810
00:50:56,679 --> 00:50:58,305
What have you got to be sorry about ?

811
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:02,601
My mother ? Don 't waste your time .

812
00:51:02,643 --> 00:51:06,355
She ditched us when I was 11 and ran off with some hotel man in the east .

813
00:51:07,064 --> 00:51:09,400
You know what a mother 's love is ?

814
00:51:11,485 --> 00:51:12,653
Yes , I do .

815
00:51:13,487 --> 00:51:14,989
You mean it 's better to be ditched ?

816
00:51:16,824 --> 00:51:21,662
No . I think it 's better to be loved . Don 't you ever see her ?

817
00:51:27,334 --> 00:51:28,794
( VOICE BREAKING ) I don 't know where she is .

818
00:51:32,673 --> 00:51:36,260
Well , maybe I ought to go join the other children .

819
00:51:42,349 --> 00:51:44,143
ANNIE : All right . Here we go . One ...

820
00:51:46,520 --> 00:51:47,980
Two ...

821
00:51:49,231 --> 00:51:50,816
Three ...

822
00:51:51,817 --> 00:51:53,902
There you go .

823
00:51:53,986 --> 00:51:56,155
( CHILDREN SQUEALING EXCITEDLY )

824
00:51:56,196 --> 00:51:57,948
( CHILDREN LAUGHING )

825
00:52:02,870 --> 00:52:04,371
BOY : Look ! Look !

826
00:52:05,706 --> 00:52:08,250
Hey ! No touching allowed !

827
00:52:08,334 --> 00:52:09,835
( SQUAWKING )

828
00:52:09,877 --> 00:52:11,378
Oh !

829
00:52:11,462 --> 00:52:12,671
( BIRDS SQUAWKING )

830
00:52:16,300 --> 00:52:17,718
( CHILDREN SCREAMING )

831
00:52:21,180 --> 00:52:22,181
( LOUD POP )

832
00:52:37,905 --> 00:52:39,448
Help me get the children into the house .

833
00:53:15,442 --> 00:53:17,403
There you go .

834
00:53:19,154 --> 00:53:21,156
( SOBBING )

835
00:53:22,950 --> 00:53:24,576
Have they gone , Mitch ?

836
00:53:24,618 --> 00:53:25,786
I think so .

837
00:53:25,869 --> 00:53:26,995
LYDIA : Is anyone hurt ?

838
00:53:27,079 --> 00:53:29,832
WOMAN : Jenny got a scratch down her cheek , but it 's nothing .

839
00:53:29,915 --> 00:53:32,292
That makes three times .

840
00:53:35,879 --> 00:53:38,382
Mitch , this isn 't usual , is it ?

841
00:53:38,465 --> 00:53:40,592
The gull when I was in the boat yesterday ,

842
00:53:40,634 --> 00:53:42,386
the one at Annie 's last night , and now ...

843
00:53:42,469 --> 00:53:44,096
Last night ? What do you mean ?

844
00:53:44,138 --> 00:53:48,600
A gull smashed into Annie 's front door . Mitch , what 's happening ?

845
00:53:48,642 --> 00:53:51,854
I don 't know . Do you have to go back to Annie 's ?

846
00:53:51,937 --> 00:53:53,480
No . I have my things in the car .

847
00:53:53,522 --> 00:53:57,192
Stay and have something to eat before you start back . I 'd feel a lot better .

848
00:54:08,328 --> 00:54:09,830
Would you like some mustard with that ?

849
00:54:09,872 --> 00:54:11,540
MELANIE : No , thank you .

850
00:54:11,623 --> 00:54:12,916
Why didn 't Annie stay for dinner ?

851
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:14,293
Said something about going home

852
00:54:14,334 --> 00:54:15,878
to take a call from her sister in the east .

853
00:54:15,961 --> 00:54:17,963
- ( CHIRPING ) - What 's the matter with them ?

854
00:54:18,005 --> 00:54:19,590
What 's the matter with all the birds ?

855
00:54:19,673 --> 00:54:21,300
Where did you want this coffee ?

856
00:54:21,341 --> 00:54:22,676
Here on the table , honey .

857
00:54:22,718 --> 00:54:24,470
Hurry up with yours , Mitch .

858
00:54:24,511 --> 00:54:27,222
I 'm sure Miss Daniels wants to be on her way .

859
00:54:27,306 --> 00:54:29,725
I think you ought to stay the night , Melanie .

860
00:54:29,808 --> 00:54:32,811
We have an extra room upstairs and everything .

861
00:54:32,853 --> 00:54:35,397
That road can be a pretty bad one at night , too .

862
00:54:35,481 --> 00:54:36,690
If I go across to Santa Rosa ,

863
00:54:36,774 --> 00:54:39,151
I 'll come out on the freeway much earlier , won 't I ?

864
00:54:39,193 --> 00:54:41,153
Yes , and the freeway is much quicker .

865
00:54:41,195 --> 00:54:43,405
But she 'll be hitting all the heavy traffic going back to San Francisco .

866
00:54:43,489 --> 00:54:44,531
( LOUD CHIRPING )

867
00:54:44,573 --> 00:54:47,034
CATHY : Just listen to those lovebirds .

868
00:54:47,117 --> 00:54:48,952
( CHIRPING STOPS ) ( TWITTERING )

869
00:54:49,036 --> 00:54:50,037
MELANIE : Mitch .

870
00:54:56,168 --> 00:54:57,836
( BIRDS SCREECHING )

871
00:55:02,674 --> 00:55:05,552
Cover your faces ! Cover your eyes !

872
00:56:24,715 --> 00:56:26,884
That 's a sparrow , all right .

873
00:56:26,967 --> 00:56:28,635
We know what it is , Al .

874
00:56:28,677 --> 00:56:30,554
Did you have a light burning or something ?

875
00:56:30,637 --> 00:56:31,930
Yes , but there wouldn 't have been

876
00:56:31,972 --> 00:56:33,682
that much light going up the chimney .

877
00:56:33,765 --> 00:56:36,184
' Cause sometimes birds are attracted by light , you know .

878
00:56:36,268 --> 00:56:37,644
Sure is a peculiar thing .

879
00:56:37,686 --> 00:56:40,314
Well , all right , but we 've got to do something about it !

880
00:56:40,355 --> 00:56:43,650
I don 't think I get you , Mitch . Do about what ?

881
00:56:44,818 --> 00:56:47,029
MITCH : Well , the birds invaded the house .

882
00:56:47,112 --> 00:56:48,697
AL : What 's more likely , they got in the room

883
00:56:48,780 --> 00:56:50,032
and was just panicked . That 's all .

884
00:56:50,115 --> 00:56:52,242
MITCH : All right , I 'll admit a bird will panic in an enclosed room ,

885
00:56:52,326 --> 00:56:56,163
but they didn 't just get in . They came in , right down the chimney .

886
00:56:56,246 --> 00:56:58,832
AL : My wife found a bird in the back seat of her car once .

887
00:56:58,874 --> 00:57:00,375
Tell him about the party .

888
00:57:00,459 --> 00:57:03,337
That 's right . We had a party here this afternoon for Cathy , for her birthday .

889
00:57:03,378 --> 00:57:04,546
AL : How old is she ?

890
00:57:04,630 --> 00:57:05,923
MITCH : Eleven ! In the middle of the party ,

891
00:57:06,006 --> 00:57:08,592
some seagulls came down at the children !

892
00:57:08,675 --> 00:57:11,178
Miss Daniels was attacked by a gull only yesterday .

893
00:57:11,219 --> 00:57:14,681
AL : Yeah . Were the kids bothering the birds or something ?

894
00:57:14,723 --> 00:57:16,808
' Cause if you make any kind of a disturbance near them ,

895
00:57:16,850 --> 00:57:17,893
they 'll just come after you .

896
00:57:17,976 --> 00:57:22,147
Al , the children were playing a game . Those gulls attacked .

897
00:57:22,189 --> 00:57:25,651
AL : Now , Lydia , " attack " is a pretty strong word , don 't you think ?

898
00:57:25,692 --> 00:57:28,028
I mean , birds just don 't go around attacking people

899
00:57:28,070 --> 00:57:29,947
without no reason . You know what I mean ?

900
00:57:30,030 --> 00:57:32,866
The kids probably scared them , that 's all .

901
00:57:32,908 --> 00:57:34,701
These birds attacked .

902
00:57:35,744 --> 00:57:39,498
You got quite a mess here , I 'll admit that .

903
00:57:39,539 --> 00:57:42,209
Maybe you ought to put some screen on top of your chimney .

904
00:57:42,292 --> 00:57:43,335
You want some help cleaning up ?

905
00:57:43,377 --> 00:57:44,544
- MITCH : No . I can handle it . - ( GASPS )

906
00:57:44,586 --> 00:57:46,713
It shouldn 't be too much of a job .

907
00:57:49,675 --> 00:57:51,760
I 'll take Cathy up to bed .

908
00:57:52,970 --> 00:57:55,389
I think I should stay , don 't you ?

909
00:57:55,430 --> 00:57:56,932
MITCH : It would be nice if you could .

910
00:57:58,767 --> 00:57:59,893
My things are in the car .

911
00:57:59,977 --> 00:58:01,436
- Do you want to go with me ? - All right .

912
00:58:01,520 --> 00:58:02,854
AL : Well , anything else I can do , Mitch ?

913
00:58:02,896 --> 00:58:03,939
MITCH : No , thanks , Al .

914
00:58:04,022 --> 00:58:05,065
We 'll be all right .

915
00:58:05,107 --> 00:58:06,608
Good night , Lydia .

916
00:58:06,692 --> 00:58:09,319
Sure is peculiar .

917
00:58:12,948 --> 00:58:14,574
( SHOVEL GRATING )

918
00:58:19,913 --> 00:58:24,042
LYDIA : Mitch . Mitch . Mitch !

919
00:58:24,084 --> 00:58:25,252
MITCH : Yes , Mother ?

920
00:58:25,293 --> 00:58:27,421
LYDIA : I 'm going to drop Cathy off now .

921
00:58:27,462 --> 00:58:30,298
I 'll probably drive over to the Fawcett farm .

922
00:58:30,382 --> 00:58:31,717
- MITCH : Okay . - ( VEHICLE STARTING )

923
00:59:11,214 --> 00:59:12,466
MAN : Morning .

924
00:59:15,135 --> 00:59:17,637
Good morning , George . Is Mr. Fawcett around ?

925
00:59:17,679 --> 00:59:19,139
I think so , ma 'am .

926
00:59:19,181 --> 00:59:22,809
Ain 't seen him this morning , but he ought to be in there .

927
00:59:23,351 --> 00:59:24,644
Thanks .

928
00:59:46,458 --> 00:59:49,336
Dan , are you home ?

929
01:00:51,231 --> 01:00:52,482
( GASPING )

930
01:00:56,695 --> 01:00:57,946
( CHOKING )

931
01:01:04,327 --> 01:01:05,328
( STARTS ENGINE )

932
01:01:33,481 --> 01:01:34,774
( SOBBING )

933
01:01:38,445 --> 01:01:39,738
Mother !

934
01:01:40,780 --> 01:01:42,949
What is it , dear ? What 's the matter ?

935
01:01:54,085 --> 01:01:55,378
Al Malone , the deputy , just called .

936
01:01:55,462 --> 01:01:56,755
He wants me over at the Fawcett place .

937
01:01:56,796 --> 01:01:58,924
Some detectives from Santa Rosa will be there .

938
01:01:58,965 --> 01:02:00,300
- Will it be all right ? - Yes .

939
01:02:00,383 --> 01:02:03,261
I was just taking your mother in some tea .

940
01:02:05,305 --> 01:02:07,974
Oh , be careful , please .

941
01:02:17,859 --> 01:02:19,778
And you be careful .

942
01:02:30,538 --> 01:02:32,832
( DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES )

943
01:02:52,435 --> 01:02:53,770
( KNOCKING )

944
01:02:54,187 --> 01:02:55,355
LYDIA : Mitch ?

945
01:02:56,731 --> 01:02:58,358
No , it 's me , Mrs. Brenner .

946
01:02:58,441 --> 01:03:00,026
I thought you might like some tea .

947
01:03:00,068 --> 01:03:02,862
Oh . Thank you .

948
01:03:04,656 --> 01:03:05,907
Where 's Mitch ?

949
01:03:05,991 --> 01:03:08,368
Al Malone wanted him out at the Fawcett farm .

950
01:03:08,410 --> 01:03:11,246
Why ? Didn 't Al believe my story ?

951
01:03:11,329 --> 01:03:14,165
He was calling from the farm .

952
01:03:14,207 --> 01:03:15,709
Then he saw .

953
01:03:15,750 --> 01:03:17,002
Oh , he must have .

954
01:03:17,043 --> 01:03:19,337
They sent for the Santa Rosa police .

955
01:03:19,379 --> 01:03:21,923
What good will they do ?

956
01:03:24,926 --> 01:03:26,886
Do you think Cathy 's all right at the school ?

957
01:03:28,263 --> 01:03:29,973
Yes , I 'm sure she 's fine .

958
01:03:32,851 --> 01:03:35,061
Do I sound very foolish to you ?

959
01:03:35,562 --> 01:03:37,063
Oh , no .

960
01:03:40,567 --> 01:03:42,902
I keep seeing Dan 's face .

961
01:03:42,944 --> 01:03:45,280
And they have such big windows at the school .

962
01:03:45,363 --> 01:03:47,407
All the windows are broken in Dan 's bedroom .

963
01:03:47,866 --> 01:03:49,034
All the windows !

964
01:03:49,075 --> 01:03:51,369
Try not to think about that .

965
01:03:52,746 --> 01:03:55,665
I wish I were a stronger person .

966
01:04:00,086 --> 01:04:03,131
I lost my husband four years ago , you know .

967
01:04:05,091 --> 01:04:08,762
It 's terrible how you depend on someone else for strength , and then

968
01:04:10,597 --> 01:04:13,767
suddenly all the strength is gone , and you 're alone .

969
01:04:19,272 --> 01:04:22,067
I 'd love to be able to relax sometime .

970
01:04:22,942 --> 01:04:25,653
I 'd love to be able to sleep .

971
01:04:28,114 --> 01:04:29,616
Do you think Cathy 's all right ?

972
01:04:29,699 --> 01:04:31,576
Annie 's there .

973
01:04:31,618 --> 01:04:33,411
She 'll be all right .

974
01:04:36,039 --> 01:04:39,376
I 'm not like this , you know ? Not usually .

975
01:04:39,459 --> 01:04:42,212
I don 't fuss and fret about my children .

976
01:04:46,549 --> 01:04:48,301
When Frank died ...

977
01:04:50,887 --> 01:04:54,974
You see , he understood the children . He really understood them .

978
01:04:55,058 --> 01:04:58,728
He had the knack of entering into their world and becoming part of them .

979
01:04:59,354 --> 01:05:01,189
That 's a very rare talent .

980
01:05:01,272 --> 01:05:02,357
Yes .

981
01:05:04,984 --> 01:05:07,612
Oh , I wish , I wish , I wish I could be like that .

982
01:05:11,574 --> 01:05:12,867
I miss him .

983
01:05:15,870 --> 01:05:18,957
Sometimes , even now , I wake up in the morning and I think ,

984
01:05:19,833 --> 01:05:22,669
" I must get Frank 's breakfast . "

985
01:05:23,336 --> 01:05:27,006
And I get up , and there 's a very good reason for getting out of bed ,

986
01:05:27,090 --> 01:05:29,175
until , of course ,

987
01:05:29,676 --> 01:05:31,010
I remember .

988
01:05:36,724 --> 01:05:38,935
I miss talking to him .

989
01:05:40,854 --> 01:05:43,565
Cathy 's a child , of course , and Mitch ...

990
01:05:45,525 --> 01:05:49,154
Well , Mitch has his own life .

991
01:05:50,780 --> 01:05:52,240
I 'm glad he stayed here today .

992
01:05:52,323 --> 01:05:55,076
I feel safer with him here .

993
01:05:56,786 --> 01:05:58,371
Would you like to rest now ?

994
01:05:58,455 --> 01:05:59,622
No .

995
01:05:59,706 --> 01:06:02,000
No , don 't go .

996
01:06:03,877 --> 01:06:06,254
I feel as if I don 't understand you at all ,

997
01:06:06,337 --> 01:06:08,506
and I want so much to understand .

998
01:06:09,215 --> 01:06:10,508
Why , Mrs. Brenner ?

999
01:06:13,219 --> 01:06:17,056
Because my son seems to be very fond of you ,

1000
01:06:17,140 --> 01:06:19,309
and I don 't quite know how I feel about it .

1001
01:06:23,271 --> 01:06:25,231
I don 't even know if I like you or not .

1002
01:06:28,067 --> 01:06:30,904
Is that so important , your liking me ?

1003
01:06:30,945 --> 01:06:32,906
Well , yes . I think so .

1004
01:06:34,157 --> 01:06:36,743
Mitch is important to me .

1005
01:06:36,784 --> 01:06:39,370
I want to like whatever girl he chooses .

1006
01:06:41,331 --> 01:06:42,707
And perhaps if you don 't ?

1007
01:06:44,501 --> 01:06:48,630
Well , then I don 't think it 'll matter very much to anyone but me .

1008
01:06:49,088 --> 01:06:51,299
Oh , I think it would also matter to Mitch .

1009
01:06:52,884 --> 01:06:55,845
Mitch has always done exactly what he wanted to do .

1010
01:07:00,725 --> 01:07:03,269
But , you see ,

1011
01:07:04,771 --> 01:07:06,439
I don 't want to be left alone .

1012
01:07:06,898 --> 01:07:09,400
I don 't think I could bear to be left alone !

1013
01:07:09,442 --> 01:07:11,486
Oh , forgive me .

1014
01:07:12,320 --> 01:07:14,447
Oh , forgive me .

1015
01:07:14,531 --> 01:07:17,116
This business with the birds has upset me .

1016
01:07:17,200 --> 01:07:20,620
I don 't know what I 'd do if Mitch weren 't here .

1017
01:07:20,662 --> 01:07:23,915
Why don 't you try to sleep now , Mrs. Brenner ?

1018
01:07:24,999 --> 01:07:27,335
I wish I was stronger .

1019
01:07:31,297 --> 01:07:33,091
Do you think she 's all right ?

1020
01:07:33,132 --> 01:07:35,093
Do you think she 's all right at the school ?

1021
01:07:36,553 --> 01:07:38,137
Would you like me to go for her ?

1022
01:07:38,638 --> 01:07:41,140
Oh , I couldn 't ask it .

1023
01:07:41,224 --> 01:07:42,934
Oh , I don 't mind , really .

1024
01:07:43,810 --> 01:07:45,478
Would you ?

1025
01:07:45,562 --> 01:07:47,272
I 'd feel so much better .

1026
01:07:47,313 --> 01:07:49,148
I 'll go right now .

1027
01:07:59,075 --> 01:08:00,827
Melanie ?

1028
01:08:03,329 --> 01:08:05,248
