Listen , get some water , bandages , and antiseptic . Quickly !

1521
01:50:09,478 --> 01:50:11,772
Bandages . It 's terrible .

1522
01:50:15,776 --> 01:50:17,736
Cathy , get some brandy .

1523
01:50:29,206 --> 01:50:31,875
No , no , no ! No , no , it 's all right .

1524
01:50:31,917 --> 01:50:33,877
No , it 's all right , it 's all right , it 's all right .

1525
01:50:33,919 --> 01:50:37,005
It 's all right . It 's all right . No .

1526
01:50:37,047 --> 01:50:38,799
- ( GASPING ) - ( SHUSHING )

1527
01:51:04,950 --> 01:51:06,910
Cathy , get the lamp .

1528
01:51:21,466 --> 01:51:23,969
( SIGHS ) We 've got to get her to a hospital .

1529
01:51:24,052 --> 01:51:25,762
We can 't , Mitch . There 's no place we can go .

1530
01:51:25,804 --> 01:51:26,805
There 's San Francisco .

1531
01:51:26,930 --> 01:51:27,931
We 'd never make it .

1532
01:51:27,973 --> 01:51:29,266
We have to try .

1533
01:51:29,349 --> 01:51:30,893
We 'll go by way of Bay Hill Road .

1534
01:51:30,934 --> 01:51:32,436
Then we don 't have to go through town .

1535
01:51:32,519 --> 01:51:34,438
We can 't stay here . She needs help !

1536
01:51:35,105 --> 01:51:37,357
I 'm frightened . Terribly frightened .

1537
01:51:39,318 --> 01:51:41,069
I don 't know what 's outside there .

1538
01:51:42,446 --> 01:51:45,574
We better get started before another attack comes .

1539
01:51:45,616 --> 01:51:48,368
We 'll take Melanie 's car . That 'll be faster than the truck .

1540
01:51:48,452 --> 01:51:49,828
Can you finish the bandaging ?

1541
01:51:49,912 --> 01:51:51,038
I 'll try .

1542
01:51:51,121 --> 01:51:52,456
All right .

1543
01:51:59,213 --> 01:52:03,800
LYDIA : Mitch ? See if you can get anything on the car radio .

1544
01:52:09,806 --> 01:52:11,308
( SOFT COOING )

1545
01:52:41,088 --> 01:52:42,506
( FLUTTERING )

1546
01:52:51,348 --> 01:52:52,557
( CAWING )

1547
01:53:30,679 --> 01:53:32,139
( LOW CLATTER )

1548
01:54:00,917 --> 01:54:02,919
( SWITCHING STATIONS )

1549
01:54:03,003 --> 01:54:05,589
ANNOUNCER : The bird attacks have subsided for the time being .

1550
01:54:05,630 --> 01:54:07,049
Bodega Bay seems to be the center ,

1551
01:54:07,090 --> 01:54:08,759
though there are reports of minor attacks

1552
01:54:08,800 --> 01:54:11,887
on Sebastopol and a few on Santa Rosa .

1553
01:54:11,928 --> 01:54:14,431
Bodega Bay has been cordoned off by roadblocks .

1554
01:54:14,514 --> 01:54:16,475
Most of the townspeople have managed to get out ,

1555
01:54:16,558 --> 01:54:19,227
but there are still some isolated pockets of people .

1556
01:54:19,269 --> 01:54:22,898
No decision has been arrived at yet as to what the next step will be ,

1557
01:54:22,939 --> 01:54:26,109
but there 's been some discussion as to whether the military should go in .

1558
01:54:26,193 --> 01:54:28,070
It appears that the bird attacks come in waves ,

1559
01:54:28,111 --> 01:54:29,863
with long intervals between .

1560
01:54:29,946 --> 01:54:32,991
The reason for this does not seem clear as yet .

1561
01:55:09,820 --> 01:55:11,321
( STARTS ENGINE )

1562
01:55:13,156 --> 01:55:15,283
( MOTOR TURNING OVER SLOWLY )

1563
01:55:31,007 --> 01:55:32,134
( SHUTS OFF MOTOR )

1564
01:55:32,175 --> 01:55:33,969
( HAND BRAKE CLICKS )

1565
01:56:23,935 --> 01:56:26,021
Did you hear anything on the radio ?

1566
01:56:26,062 --> 01:56:28,565
It 's all right . Come on .

1567
01:56:51,755 --> 01:56:53,423
( TURNS DOOR KNOB )

1568
01:57:02,974 --> 01:57:04,434
( GULL CRYING )

1569
01:57:07,062 --> 01:57:09,272
No . No !

1570
01:57:09,356 --> 01:57:10,690
( HUSHING )

1571
01:57:38,760 --> 01:57:39,970
Mitch ?

1572
01:57:40,512 --> 01:57:41,596
Shh .

1573
01:57:42,138 --> 01:57:43,473
Stay there .

1574
01:57:51,398 --> 01:57:53,733
Can I bring the lovebirds , Mitch ?

1575
01:57:53,817 --> 01:57:56,069
They haven 't harmed anyone .

1576
01:57:56,152 --> 01:57:58,321
All right . Bring them .

1577
01:58:40,322 --> 01:58:41,865
( STARTS ENGINE )

1578
01:58:50,248 --> 01:58:52,250
( BIRD CAWING INTENSIFIES )

